### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Session 1 - basic reads
### Open this file in VS Code / BAS with the "REST Client" extension
### and click "Send Request" above each request. Run `cds watch` first.
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

@server = http://localhost:4004
@vendorId = a1b2c3d4-0000-0000-0000-000000000002

### Service document - lists all entity sets
GET {{server}}/odata/v4/vendor/

### Service metadata (EDMX) - the OData "contract", similar to a WSDL
GET {{server}}/odata/v4/vendor/$metadata

### All vendors (Pending vendors show " (pending)" - added by the after READ handler)
GET {{server}}/odata/v4/vendor/Vendors

### One vendor by key
GET {{server}}/odata/v4/vendor/Vendors(a1b2c3d4-0000-0000-0000-000000000001)

### Vendors with their contacts (deep read via composition)
GET {{server}}/odata/v4/vendor/Vendors?$expand=contacts

### Filter + select + order
GET {{server}}/odata/v4/vendor/Vendors?$filter=status eq 'Active'&$select=name,country&$orderby=name


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
### Session 2 - custom logic, actions, functions
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### Create WITHOUT name -> expect 400 "Vendor name is required"
POST {{server}}/odata/v4/vendor/Vendors
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "country": "US"
}

### Create a vendor -> expect 201, status defaults to "Pending"
POST {{server}}/odata/v4/vendor/Vendors
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "New Vendor Ltd",
  "country": "GB",
  "website": "https://newvendor.example.com"
}

### Deep create: vendor + contacts in one request
POST {{server}}/odata/v4/vendor/Vendors
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Deep Insert Inc",
  "country": "CA",
  "contacts": [
    { "name": "Alice Brown", "email": "alice@deepinsert.example.com" },
    { "name": "Bob White",   "email": "bob@deepinsert.example.com" }
  ]
}

### Activate a Pending vendor (bound action) -> status becomes "Active"
POST {{server}}/odata/v4/vendor/Vendors({{vendorId}})/VendorService.activate
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### Read-only view: only Active vendors
GET {{server}}/odata/v4/vendor/ActiveVendors

### Try to write to the read-only view -> expect 405
POST {{server}}/odata/v4/vendor/ActiveVendors
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Should Fail"
}

### Unbound function: number of vendors
GET {{server}}/odata/v4/vendor/vendorCount()

### Vendors with contacts again
GET {{server}}/odata/v4/vendor/Vendors?$expand=contacts
